      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I was going to open a feature request for that.\n\nMy upcoming avatar is using this packing of channels on the PC version :\n\n- AlbedoSmoothness (RGB+A) : BC7 and high resolution\n\n- MetalOcclusion (R+G) : BC1 at low resolution\n\nUnity Standard allow to pack the smoothness in the albedo for very good reasons :\n\n- Most materials don't need a metal map and if you don't use an occlusion map you have one less texture which is a serious performance gain especially on mobile.\n\n- So far in my work the smoothness map had much more details than the metal and occlusion maps. This is common enough that Unity Standard supports it.\n\n- I am not familiar with Unity shaders but IIRC this switch is optimized at compile time so it is basically free.\n\n- Probably rather easy to add and low maintenance after the act.\n\nVRChat's \"Standard\" replacement should supports this feature like its Unity counterpart, especially since it allows to make mobile friendlier avatars by applying good practices the later allow.\n\nI also tried to reproduce Standard Lite with Toon Standard as a workaround but I have not figured out how to get an equivalent look.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
